<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.3.4">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml" /><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" /><updated>2026-05-29T10:27:44+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/feed.xml</id><title type="html">The Best Running Podcasts</title><subtitle>An independent, hand-curated directory of the best running podcasts—road, track, trail, ultra, skyrunning, and training science. Each entry is reviewed for quality and usefulness for runners, coaches, and fans. Filter by training focus and language, discover Spotify and Apple Podcasts links, and find shows worth your long run.
</subtitle><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><entry><title type="html">Ultrarunning History</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/ultrarunning-history-podcast.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Ultrarunning History" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/ultrarunning-history-podcast</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/ultrarunning-history-podcast.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A podcast about the history of ultrarunning by ultrarunner and historian Davy Crocket.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">The Way Of The Runner</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-way-of-the-runner.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="The Way Of The Runner" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-way-of-the-runner</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-way-of-the-runner.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Award-winning author Adharanand Finn talks to runners of every kind about the joy and experience of running.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Trail Runner Nation</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/trail-runner-nation.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Trail Runner Nation" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/trail-runner-nation</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/trail-runner-nation.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Trail Runner Nation is devoted to sharing knowledge and advice to the trail running community - from beginners to the pros! Tips and discussions regarding race nutrition, pacing strategy, mental focus and much more from well-respected members of the trail community.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">The Real Science Of Sport</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-real-science-of-sports.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="The Real Science Of Sport" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-real-science-of-sports</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-real-science-of-sports.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="track" /><category term="science" /><category term="road" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[World-renowned sports scientist Professor Ross Tucker and veteran sports journalist Mike Finch break down the myths, practices and controversies from the world of sport. They cover all sports, and 75% of the episodes have some running related content.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">The Midpacker Podcast</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-midpacker-podcast.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="The Midpacker Podcast" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-midpacker-podcast</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-midpacker-podcast.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Troy Meadows presents a podcast which follows middle and back of the pack trail runners and ultra runners at the heart of the trail running community.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Women of Distance</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/women-of-distance.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Women of Distance" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/women-of-distance</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/women-of-distance.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A podcast about the women of Mountain, Trail, Ultra and Road running worlds. Hosted by Devon Yanko.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Uphill Athlete</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/uphill-athlete.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Uphill Athlete" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/uphill-athlete</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/uphill-athlete.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="ultra" /><category term="skyrunning" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Legendary alpine climber Steve House brings you highly informative discussions that range widely across topics, including running.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">The Sub Hub</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-sub-hub.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="The Sub Hub" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-sub-hub</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-sub-hub.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="subultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Dani Moreno and and EmKay Sullivan brings you your hub for all things sub-ultra mountain and trail running.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Distance to Empty</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/distance-to-empty.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Distance to Empty" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/distance-to-empty</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/distance-to-empty.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Through in-depth interviews with athletes, race organizers and sports scientists, shedding light on the unique challenges involved in tackling 200+ mile races.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Life in Stride</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/life-in-stride.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Life in Stride" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/life-in-stride</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/life-in-stride.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="road" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Goal of the podcast: serve as a safe haven for the “try hard” amateur who loves to balance the demands of family, work and life while building their fastest self.]]></summary></entry></feed>